---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Workers fall behind" hint="Jobs arrive at 33,000 per second for 2 hours while the workers slow down, and Redis may stop accepting writes. Choose the design and how the relay is limited, and see whether jobs are refused, whether Redis fills up and where the waiting jobs sit. A simple model with round numbers, not Slack's code or data.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. With <b>Redis only</b>, workers at <b>60%</b> of normal speed for <b>45</b> minutes and <b>10</b> GB of free Redis memory, Redis is full at minute <b>47.0</b>, the workers get stuck because taking a job also needs memory, and <b>144.5</b> million jobs are refused.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Design</b> to <b>Kafka in front of Redis</b> with <b>Relay limit</b> on <b>Unlimited</b>: <b>0</b> jobs are refused, because Kafka keeps accepting them (<b>144.5</b> million wait there), but Redis still fills at minute <b>47.0</b> and the workers are stuck.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Relay limit</b> to <b>Matched to the workers</b>: Redis never passes <b>0%</b>, nothing is refused, the workers keep running, and the relay has emptied Kafka by the end.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Relay limit</b> to <b>Paused during the slowdown</b>: Redis stays at <b>0%</b> and <b>61.8</b> million jobs are still waiting in Kafka at the end.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set <b>Redis stops accepting writes (minutes)</b> to <b>15</b>: <b>29.7</b> million jobs are refused. With Kafka in front and the limit matched, <b>0</b> are refused and <b>18.6</b> million are still waiting in Kafka at the end.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg slk" data-slk>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Design <select class="pg-in" data-kafka><option value="off">Redis only</option><option value="on">Kafka in front of Redis</option></select></label>
      <label>Relay limit (needs Kafka) <select class="pg-in" data-relay><option value="matched">Matched to the workers</option><option value="unlimited">Unlimited</option><option value="paused">Paused during the slowdown</option></select></label>
      <RangeField label="Workers run at this share of normal speed (%)" name="sp" min="20" max="100" step="10" value="60" />
      <RangeField label="Slowdown lasts (minutes)" name="sl" min="0" max="90" step="5" value="45" />
      <RangeField label="Redis stops accepting writes (minutes)" name="ou" min="0" max="30" step="5" value="0" />
      <RangeField label="Free Redis memory for waiting jobs (GB)" name="hd" min="1" max="50" value="10" />
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Jobs refused when the web app tries to add them</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Redis memory, highest point</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Workers at the end</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Jobs waiting in Kafka at the end</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="slk-strip-wrap">
      <p class="pg-note slk-cap">Can the web app add jobs? One box for every 10 minutes of the 2 hours:</p>
      <ol class="slk-strip" data-strip></ol>
      <p class="pg-note">ok = every job was accepted, refused = some jobs were turned away in that period.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, invented for teaching and not Slack data: jobs arrive at 33,000 per second, Slack's peak, for 120 minutes. Workers can normally finish 40,000 jobs per second. At minute 10 they slow down for the length you set, and Redis stops accepting writes for the length you set, if any. A job takes 500 bytes. Redis holds only as many waiting jobs as the free memory allows. When it is full, workers cannot take a job either, because taking one needs a little memory, and in this model they stay stuck until someone clears Redis by hand. With Redis only, the web app writes to Redis, so it is refused when Redis is full or not accepting writes. With Kafka in front, Kafkagate always accepts the job and the relay moves it to Redis: at most 60,000 per second when unlimited, at the workers' current speed when matched, and nothing during the slowdown when paused (then matched). While Redis is not accepting writes the relay retries and the jobs stay in Kafka, which keeps them 2 days, longer than this model runs. Real systems are more complicated than this.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .slk-strip-wrap { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .slk-cap { margin: 0; }
  .slk-strip { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 3px; }
  .slk-strip li { min-width: 6.4rem; padding: 4px 6px; display: grid; place-items: center; border-radius: 5px; font: 600 .75rem var(--font-mono); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); color: var(--text); }
  .slk-strip li[data-k='ok'] { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--good) 22%, var(--surface)); }
  .slk-strip li[data-k='refused'] { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 16%, var(--surface)); color: var(--bad-text); border-style: dashed; }
</style>
<script>
  import { query, fmt } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-slk]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const ARRIVE = 33000; // jobs per second: Slack's peak
    const NORMAL = 40000; // jobs per second the workers finish when healthy (teaching figure)
    const RELAY_MAX = 60000; // jobs per second an unlimited relay can move (teaching figure)
    const JOB_BYTES = 500, GB = 1e9, MILLION = 1e6, COPIES = 3;
    const START_S = 600; // slowdown and Redis trouble begin at minute 10
    const TOTAL_S = 7200; // 120 minutes
    const SLICE_S = 600; // one strip box per 10 minutes
    const SLICES = TOTAL_S / SLICE_S;
    const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { kafka: 'off', relay: 'matched', sp: '60', sl: '45', ou: '0', hd: '10' };
    const strip = q('[data-strip]');
    const cells = Array.from({ length: SLICES }, () => { const li = document.createElement('li'); strip.append(li); return li; });
    const mil = (n: number) => (Math.round((n / MILLION) * 10) / 10).toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 1 });
    const input = (k: string) => q<HTMLInputElement>(`[data-${k}]`);
    const select = (k: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-${k}]`);

    function draw() {
      const kafka = select('kafka').value === 'on'; const relay = select('relay').value;
      const speed = Number(input('sp').value); const slowMin = Number(input('sl').value);
      const outMin = Number(input('ou').value); const headGb = Number(input('hd').value);
      q('[data-spval]').textContent = String(speed); q('[data-slval]').textContent = String(slowMin);
      q('[data-ouval]').textContent = String(outMin); q('[data-hdval]').textContent = String(headGb);
      select('relay').disabled = !kafka;
      const cap = (headGb * GB) / JOB_BYTES; // waiting jobs Redis can hold
      let redis = 0, wait = 0, refused = 0, stuckAt = -1, peak = 0;
      const refusedIn = new Array(SLICES).fill(false);
      for (let t = 0; t < TOTAL_S; t++) {
        const slow = t >= START_S && t < START_S + slowMin * 60;
        const rate = NORMAL * (slow ? speed / 100 : 1);
        const writable = !(t >= START_S && t < START_S + outMin * 60);
        if (!kafka) {
          const taken = writable ? Math.min(ARRIVE, Math.max(0, cap - redis)) : 0;
          if (taken < ARRIVE) { refused += ARRIVE - taken; refusedIn[Math.floor(t / SLICE_S)] = true; }
          redis += taken;
        } else {
          wait += ARRIVE;
          const limit = relay === 'unlimited' ? RELAY_MAX : relay === 'paused' && slow ? 0 : rate;
          const moved = writable ? Math.min(wait, limit, Math.max(0, cap - redis)) : 0;
          wait -= moved; redis += moved;
        }
        if (stuckAt < 0 && redis >= cap - 0.5) stuckAt = t;
        redis -= stuckAt >= 0 ? 0 : Math.min(redis, rate);
        peak = Math.max(peak, redis / cap);
      }
      const stuck = stuckAt >= 0; const stuckMin = stuckAt / 60;
      const total = ARRIVE * TOTAL_S; const peakPct = 100 * peak;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${mil(refused)} million`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = refused > 0 ? `${fmt((100 * refused) / total)}% of the ${mil(total)} million jobs that arrived` : (kafka ? 'Kafka accepted every job' : 'every job was accepted');
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${fmt(peakPct)}% of free memory`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = stuck ? `Redis was full from minute ${stuckMin.toFixed(1)}` : 'Redis never filled up';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = stuck ? 'stuck' : 'running';
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = stuck ? 'Redis is full, and taking a job needs memory too, so nothing can drain until it is cleared by hand' : 'workers kept taking jobs';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = kafka ? `${mil(wait)} million` : 'no Kafka';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = kafka ? `${fmt((wait * JOB_BYTES * COPIES) / GB)} GB with ${COPIES} copies, kept for up to 2 days` : 'in this design waiting jobs can only sit in Redis';
      const bad = [refused > 0, stuck, stuck, false];
      ['b1', 'b2', 'b3', 'b4'].forEach((b, i) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-${b}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad[i] ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'));
      cells.forEach((c, i) => { const k = refusedIn[i] ? 'refused' : 'ok'; c.textContent = `${i * 10}–${(i + 1) * 10} min: ${k}`; c.dataset.k = k; });
      const nBad = refusedIn.filter(Boolean).length;
      strip.setAttribute('aria-label', `${nBad} of ${SLICES} ten-minute periods had refused jobs`);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const failed = refused > 0 || stuck; out.classList.toggle('bad', failed);
      if (!failed) out.textContent = `Nothing broke: no job was refused, Redis never filled up and the workers kept running.${kafka && wait > 0 ? ` ${mil(wait)} million jobs are still waiting safely in Kafka.` : ''}`;
      else if (!kafka) out.textContent = `${mil(refused)} million jobs were refused${stuck ? `, and Redis filled at minute ${stuckMin.toFixed(1)} and stuck the workers` : ' while Redis was not accepting writes'}. Put Kafka in front so the web app can keep adding jobs.`;
      else if (stuck) out.textContent = `Kafka kept accepting jobs, but the relay filled Redis at minute ${stuckMin.toFixed(1)} and the workers are stuck. Set the relay limit to match the workers so Redis never fills.`;
      else out.textContent = `${mil(refused)} million jobs were refused.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      ['kafka', 'relay'].forEach((k) => (select(k).value = DEFAULTS[k]));
      ['sp', 'sl', 'ou', 'hd'].forEach((k) => (input(k).value = DEFAULTS[k]));
      draw();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
